<rml>
<head>
    <title>Match options</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="look.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="dialog.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="room.rcss"/>
</head>
<!-- Port-only (SPEC-menus.md's stage 4, "MATCH OPTIONS"): a window over the room: FORCES, PLAY and WEAPONS down its side,
     the tab's options beside them, each with the value the match plays. The host's are switches and steppers, sent as
     they change; a guest's are their values, with "The host sets these.". An option a player's game doesn't have says
     whose. DONE (the host's) or CLOSE (a guest's) goes back to the room. The rows are the game's (MATCH OPTIONS' rows,
     logistics/MCMatchOptionsTab), put in by logistics/MCMatchOptionsWindow. -->
<body class="window-body">
    <div class="veil"></div>
    <div class="window-place">
        <div id="options" class="panel glass">
            <div class="panel-name">Match options</div>
            <div class="options-body">
                <div class="side-tabs tabs" id="tabs"><div class="side-tab tab now">Forces</div><div class="side-tab tab">Play</div><div class="side-tab tab">Weapons</div></div>
                <div class="set-rows" id="rows"></div>
            </div>
            <div class="options-foot"><div class="note" id="note">The host sets these.</div><div class="grow"></div>
                <div class="button main" id="done" data-hint="Done">Done</div></div>
            <div class="hints row"><div class="mouse-hints grow"></div><div class="keys"></div></div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
